NAME
       chmod, chown - change permissions and ownership

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/stat.h>
       #include <unistd.h>

       int chmod(const char *path, mode_t mode);
       int chown(const char *path, uid_t uid, gid_t gid);

DESCRIPTION
       chmod sets the permission bits, chown the owner and group.
       Giving a file away requires root.

       The execute bit is enforced: execve refuses a file without it,
       so a fresh script has to be made executable before it will run,
       whether or not it has a #! line.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   the path does not exist
       EPERM    the caller does not own the file, or is not root

SEE ALSO
       chmod(1), chown(1), execve(2), stat(2)
